# Version history

## 2026-10-24

- Phase 8: Restore & verify — browse task cycles, point-in-time file restore to a folder, unzip archived cycles on demand, and verify archive zip integrity.

## 2026-10-23

- History: click a run to open a detail panel with live progress bar and terminal-style log stream (persisted run logs + IPC progress/log events).
- Fixed MySQL/MariaDB dump: prefer `mariadb-dump`, disable client TLS by default (`--ssl=0`) for non-TLS servers; optional profile “Require SSL/TLS”.
- Fixed Driver Manager install `fetch failed` by downloading via Node https/http (with redirects and clearer network errors) instead of Electron fetch.
- Phase 7: Driver Manager (download/extract from drivers.taam.shop, SHA-256 meta) + database dump backups (mysqldump, pg_dump, mongodump, sqlpackage .bacpac, SQLite copy) with SSH tunnel support.
- Fixed S3-compatible Test Connection `UnknownError` (Arvan/MinIO): normalize bucket-in-hostname endpoints, default path-style + disable flexible checksums, HeadBucket→ListObjects fallback, clearer error text.
- Phase 6: AWS S3 / S3-compatible source adapter — list objects by prefix, download into cycle layout, ETag-aware manifests; profile bucket + optional object prefix (`remotePath`).

## 2026-10-22

- Phase 5: SFTP / FTP / SSH-via-SFTP source adapters — recursive list + download into baseline/changes, exclude patterns, `remotePath` on file profiles; **Run now** performs a real transfer for those types.
- Phase 4: backup engine core — run planner (full/period/changes/rollover), cycle layout + manifest, zip finalize, retention prune, worker that claims pending runs; History screen lists runs.
- Tasks: **Run now** queues a real backup for SFTP/FTP/SSH (other sources wait for later phases).
- Phase 3: task CRUD wizard (source/target, schedule, backup settings), croner scheduler with timezone next-run previews, Dashboard upcoming runs, and pending run queue for Phase 4.
- Official driver mirror set to https://drivers.taam.shop/drivers/ (`src/shared/driversMirror.ts`, `driver-mirror/HOSTED_LINKS.json`).
- Fixed SSH Test Connection handshake timeouts caused by the host-key trust dialog racing a 15s readyTimeout; interactive SSH waits up to 2 minutes and focuses the Trust dialog.
- Database profiles (MySQL/MariaDB/Postgres/MSSQL/MongoDB) can connect via an SSH/SFTP jump-host profile (local port forward + Test Connection).

## 2026-10-21

- Migrated local SQLite access to Drizzle ORM (schema, migrator in `/drizzle`, typed settings/health queries).
- Fixed missing `window.backupHub` by setting `webPreferences.sandbox: false` (electron-vite bundled preload is incompatible with Electron process sandbox).
- Fixed Linux Electron startup when `chrome-sandbox` lacks root/SUID (default `--no-sandbox` on Linux; optional SUID setup documented).
- Fixed Vue template typing so `window.backupHub` calls run from script helpers (vue-tsc clean).
- Added `driver-mirror/` Python packager to download official CLI drivers (sqlpackage, MongoDB tools, PostgreSQL, MariaDB/mysqldump, 7-Zip) with SHA-256 manifests for re-hosting.
- Confirmed MSSQL strategy: prioritize sqlpackage `.bacpac` (client-side); native `.bak` deferred.
- Switched renderer UI from React to Vue 3 (`@vitejs/plugin-vue`, `vue-tsc`).
- Documented that SSH host-key trust (`ssh_host_keys`) and safeStorage credential encryption are both required for server connections.
- Phase 1 scaffold: electron-vite + Vue 3 + TypeScript BackupHub app shell.
- Secure IPC skeleton with Zod validation, typed preload `window.backupHub` API.
- better-sqlite3 database with initial migrations (profiles, tasks, runs, cycles, manifests, settings, SSH host keys).
- Pino rotating file logging under userData/logs.
- System tray, single-instance lock, close-to-tray, and Settings screen persistence.
- electron-builder targets: NSIS (Windows), DMG (macOS), AppImage + deb (Linux).
- Vitest unit tests for paths, settings schemas, and IPC channel invariants.
